%% Source basis: Lecture 3/4 and Intel MCS-51 User's Manual [2]
flowchart TB
    A[Main program executes at PC = return address]
    B[Eligible interrupt accepted at instruction boundary]
    C[Hardware-generated LCALL]
    D[Push interrupted PC high and low bytes onto internal-RAM stack]
    E[Load PC with source vector address]
    F[Vector transfers to ISR]
    G[ISR pushes ACC, PSW, B and used registers as needed]
    H[ISR identifies cause and services event]
    I[ISR clears or acknowledges flag according to derivative rules]
    J[ISR pops saved registers in reverse order]
    K[RETI marks current interrupt complete]
    L[RETI pops PC and decreases SP by two]
    M[Main program resumes at saved return address]
    N[Important: hardware LCALL does not automatically save PSW or all registers]
    A --> B --> C --> D --> E --> F --> G --> H --> I --> J --> K --> L --> M
    D -.-> N
